AI bots made an average of 4.2% of HTML requests across Cloudflare's customer base from 1 January to 2 December 2025, and Anthropic's crawl-to-refer ratio on Cloudflare's network reached as much as 500,000:1. Both figures come from the [Cloudflare Radar 2025 Year in Review](https://blog.cloudflare.com/radar-2025-year-in-review/), published on 15 December 2025. Cloudflare is a vendor measuring its own network, so these are not figures for the whole web.

_Last checked: 24 November 2026. Every figure below was read from the publication it links to. Each one describes one company's network or hosted sites in one period._

## At a glance

1. **AI bots made an average 4.2% of HTML requests on Cloudflare's customer base in 2025.** The share ran from 2.4% in early April to 6.4% in late June. Googlebot alone made 4.5% ([Cloudflare, 15 December 2025](https://blog.cloudflare.com/radar-2025-year-in-review/)).
2. **Anthropic's crawl-to-refer ratio reached as much as 500,000:1 in 2025.** After May it ranged from about 25,000:1 to about 100,000:1. OpenAI reached as much as 3,700:1 in March. Perplexity's peaks were generally below 400:1 and below 200:1 from September (same source).
3. **Training is the largest crawl purpose.** Over the 12 months to July 2025 Cloudflare put AI crawling at 80% training, 18% search and 2% user actions ([Cloudflare, 29 August 2025](https://blog.cloudflare.com/crawlers-click-ai-bots-training/)). By June 2026 Cloudflare said 52% of the crawler requests it saw were for AI training, up from 22% in spring 2025 ([Cloudflare, 30 September 2026](https://blog.cloudflare.com/agentic-web/)).
4. **Vercel's network logged 569 million GPTBot requests against 4.5 billion from Googlebot.** That was one month before 17 December 2024 ([Vercel and MERJ](https://vercel.com/blog/the-rise-of-the-ai-crawler)).

